# The sandbox with no window: what this build wired, and whether the projects load.
#
#     cd apps/sandbox
#     haxe console.hxml
#
# Seconds rather than minutes, because it is the same host without lime, openfl, flixel or a window
# under it, so it answers "is the setup right" separately from "does the app build", which are the
# two questions that otherwise get debugged as one.
#
# In a checkout of this repository, point the haxelib at it first, so `-lib hxscript` resolves and
# `extraParams.hxml` applies. That file is the whole of the setup:
#
#     haxelib dev hxscript ../..
#
# Add libraries and they are wired, because a preset keys off the define that `-lib` already sets.
# This is the fastest way to answer "can a script reach flixel":
#
#     haxe -lib flixel -lib flixel-addons --macro flixel.system.macros.FlxDefines.run() console.hxml
#
# They go *before* this file, not after it. `--run` on the last line takes everything that follows as
# arguments to the program, so a `-lib` written after it reaches Check rather than the compiler, and
# the run reports the setup it would have had without it.
#
# `--run` rather than `-main ... --interp`, because only `--run` passes arguments through. Check's own
# arguments do go after, for the same reason:
#
#     haxe console.hxml --projects ../some/other/folder

-lib hxscript
-cp .

# Names the sandbox's own classes to hxScript, so `@:scriptable` on them means something.
-D hxscript_host=host

--run Check
